[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Do You Call That a Hat?]
[00:15.40]What kind of shopping does the writer enjoy,
[00:19.25]do you think?
[00:22.75]'Do you call that a hat?' I said to my wife.
[00:28.89]'You needn't be so rude about it,'
[00:31.46]my wife answered as she looked at herself in the mirror.
[00:36.46]I sat down on one of those modern chairs with holes in it and waited.
[00:43.16]We had been in the hat shop for half an hour and my wife was still in front of the mirror.
[00:51.79]'We mustn't buy things we don't need,' I remarked suddenly.
[00:57.19]I regretted saying it almost at once.
[01:01.59]'You needn't have said that,' my wife answered.
[01:06.09]'I needn't remind you of that terrible tie you bought yesterday.'
[01:13.16]'I find it beautiful,' I said.
[01:16.49]'A man can never have too many ties.'
[01:20.58]'And a woman can't have too many hats,' she answered.
[01:26.41]Ten minutes later we walked out of the shop together.
[01:31.59]My wife was wearing a hat that looked like a lighthouse!
